  "title": "which agent writes lay the picture out fresh, and what each choice costs",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "Q1 of docs/plans/groups-in-the-layout/PLAN.md — whether a redraw that changes nothing structural still relayouts",
  "explanation": "The two options agree about everything except one kind of write: the redraw that changes only prose or a verdict. [Laying out fresh every time](#relayout-always) leaves the server with a single placement path and three helpers deleted, and costs an arrangement whenever a label gets fixed. [Laying out fresh only when the shape changed](#relayout-structural) saves that arrangement, but keeps alive the branch this whole change exists to remove. Leaves out what the new layout actually does with a group once it runs, which is the question after this one.",
  "groups": [
